      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry for the late reply. We are very close to the end of the release cycle, so I\u0027m busy making some final changes. Please forgive me if I continue to respond slowly in the next few weeks.\n\nIf I understand your problem correctly, I think the fundamental problem is that the build system incorrectly picks those arm64 assembly files when building the host libart while it really shouldn\u0027t, and that\u0027s why it asks for those arm64 assembly files to support host.\n\nTo solve this problem, you can tell the build system to use the x86_64 assembly files building the host libart.\n\nSo, instead of the current select statement:\n\n```\nselect(soong_config_variable(\"art_module\", \"art_use_simulator\"), {\n    true: [\u003cuse arm64 assembly\u003e],\n    default: [\u003cuse x86_64 assembly\u003e],\n})\n```\n\nTry this:\n\n```\nselect((soong_config_variable(\"art_module\", \"art_use_simulator\"), os()), {\n  (true, \"android\"): [\u003cuse arm64 assembly\u003e],\n  (default, default): [\u003cuse x86_64 assembly\u003e],\n})\n```",
      "parentUuid": "853357e8_6c48f2ca",
      "revId": "2e7289547bf06748a0ea72be23154bbb5ae64df0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
